    evaluate same-items of T with actual being alias, expected being [first, second, third, first], label being "rejected copy preserves destination"
    evaluate same-items of T with actual being original, expected being [first, second, third, first], label being "rejected copy preserves source"
    evaluate require with passed being ((try-copy-range of T with source being original, source-offset being 0, destination being data, destination-offset being 1, count being 2147483647) equals false), label being "copy rejects window"
    evaluate same-items of T with actual being alias, expected being [first, second, third, first], label being "rejected copy preserves destination"
    evaluate same-items of T with actual being original, expected being [first, second, third, first], label being "rejected copy preserves source"
    evaluate require with passed being ((try-copy-range of T with source being original, source-offset being minimum, destination being data, destination-offset being 0, count being 1) equals false), label being "copy rejects window"
    evaluate same-items of T with actual being alias, expected being [first, second, third, first], label being "rejected copy preserves destination"
    evaluate same-items of T with actual being original, expected being [first, second, third, first], label being "rejected copy preserves source"
    evaluate require with passed being ((try-copy-range of T with source being original, source-offset being 0, destination being data, destination-offset being minimum, count being 1) equals false), label being "copy rejects window"
    evaluate same-items of T with actual being alias, expected being [first, second, third, first], label being "rejected copy preserves destination"
    evaluate same-items of T with actual being original, expected being [first, second, third, first], label being "rejected copy preserves source"
    evaluate require with passed being ((try-copy-range of T with source being original, source-offset being 0, destination being data, destination-offset being 0, count being minimum) equals false), label being "copy rejects window"
    evaluate same-items of T with actual being alias, expected being [first, second, third, first], label being "rejected copy preserves destination"
    evaluate same-items of T with actual being original, expected being [first, second, third, first], label being "rejected copy preserves source"
    evaluate require with passed being (try-copy-range of T with source being original, source-offset being 4, destination being data, destination-offset being 4, count being 0), label being "copy endpoint"
    evaluate same-items of T with actual being alias, expected being original, label being "zero copy preserves array"
    evaluate require with passed being (try-copy-range of T with source being data, source-offset being 0, destination being alias, destination-offset being 1, count being 3), label being "overlap right"
    evaluate same-items of T with actual being alias, expected being [first, first, second, third], label being "right overlap snapshot"
    evaluate require with passed being (try-copy-range of T with source being alias, source-offset being 1, destination being data, destination-offset being 0, count being 3), label being "overlap left"
    evaluate same-items of T with actual being data, expected being [first, second, third, third], label being "left overlap snapshot"
    evaluate require with passed being (try-copy-range of T with source being alias, source-offset being 0, destination being data, destination-offset being 0, count being 4), label being "identical window"
    evaluate same-items of T with actual being data, expected being [first, second, third, third], label being "identical copy snapshot"
    value target as array of T is [third, third, third, third]
    evaluate require with passed being (try-copy-range of T with source being original, source-offset being 1, destination being target, destination-offset being 0, count being 3), label being "independent copy forward"
    evaluate same-items of T with actual being target, expected being [second, third, first, third], label being "independent forward snapshot"
    evaluate require with passed being (try-copy-range of T with source being original, source-offset being 0, destination being target, destination-offset being 1, count being 3), label being "independent copy backward"
    evaluate same-items of T with actual being target, expected being [second, first, second, third], label being "independent backward snapshot"
    evaluate same-items of T with actual being original, expected being [first, second, third, first], label being "copy leaves source"
    value short-items as array of T is [third, third]
    evaluate require with passed being ((try-copy-range of T with source being original, source-offset being 0, destination being short-items, destination-offset being 0, count being 3) equals false), label being "short destination rejects count"
    evaluate same-items of T with actual being short-items, expected being [third, third], label being "short destination keeps writable prefix"
    evaluate require with passed being (try-copy-range of T with source being original, source-offset being 0, destination being short-items, destination-offset being 0, count being 2), label being "short destination valid copy"
    evaluate same-items of T with actual being short-items, expected being [first, second], label being "short destination snapshot"
    evaluate require with passed being ((try-copy-range of T with source being short-items, source-offset being 0, destination being target, destination-offset being 0, count being 3) equals false), label being "short source rejects count"
    evaluate same-items of T with actual being target, expected being [second, first, second, third], label being "short source leaves destination"
    evaluate same-items of T with actual being short-items, expected being [first, second], label being "short source unchanged"
    evaluate require with passed being (try-copy-range of T with source being short-items, source-offset being 0, destination being target, destination-offset being 1, count being 2), label being "short source valid copy"
    evaluate same-items of T with actual being target, expected being [second, first, second, third], label being "short source valid snapshot"
    evaluate require with passed being (try-fill-range of T with items being target, offset being 0, count being 4, item-value being second), label being "fill whole array"
    evaluate same-items of T with actual being target, expected being [second, second, second, second], label being "whole fill snapshot"
    value empty as array of T is []
    value empty-result is try-get of T with items being empty, index being 0
    evaluate require with passed being (empty-result.is-none with nothing), label being "empty get"
    evaluate require with passed being ((try-set of T with items being empty, index being 0, item-value being first) equals false), label being "empty set"
    evaluate require with passed being (try-fill-range of T with items being empty, offset being 0, count being 0, item-value being first), label being "empty fill"
    evaluate require with passed being ((try-fill-range of T with items being empty, offset being 0, count being 1, item-value being first) equals false), label being "empty fill rejects item"
    evaluate require with passed being (try-copy-range of T with source being empty, source-offset being 0, destination being empty, destination-offset being 0, count being 0), label being "empty copy"
    evaluate require with passed being (try-copy-range of T with source being empty, source-offset being 0, destination being data, destination-offset being 4, count being 0), label being "empty to endpoint"
    evaluate require with passed being (try-copy-range of T with source being data, source-offset being 4, destination being empty, destination-offset being 0, count being 0), label being "endpoint to empty"
    evaluate require with passed being ((try-copy-range of T with source being empty, source-offset being 0, destination being data, destination-offset being 0, count being 1) equals false), label being "empty source rejects item"
    evaluate require with passed being ((try-copy-range of T with source being data, source-offset being 0, destination being empty, destination-offset being 0, count being 1) equals false), label being "empty destination rejects item"
    evaluate require with passed being ((the length of empty) equals 0), label being "checked operations never grow"
    say label
end paragraph

main returns override integer begin paragraph
    evaluate check-kind of override integer with first being minus 7, second being 0, third being 2147483647, label being "checked i32"
    evaluate check-kind of override long with first being (minus 9000000000 becomes override long), second being (0 becomes override long), third being (9000000000 becomes override long), label being "checked i64"
    evaluate check-kind of override byte with first being (0 becomes override byte), second being (128 becomes override byte), third being (255 becomes override byte), label being "checked u8"
    evaluate check-kind of boolean with first being true, second being false, third being true, label being "checked bool"
    evaluate check-kind of floating with first being minus 0.5, second being 0.25, third being 1.5, label being "checked f64"
    evaluate check-kind of text with first being "", second being ("middle" plus "-value"), third being "last", label being "checked text"
    give 0
end paragraph
